        "original_id": "4f4be54b-bbba-5013-95c0-5a72c4da3ce5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Auguste von Müller, Camille Saint-Saëns\n- Works: Samson et Dalila\n- Places: Weimar, Grossherzogliches Theater, Staatskapelle Weimar\n- Roles: Dalila\n\nFacts:\n- Auguste von Müller was a German operatic mezzo-soprano and actress who lived from 1848 to 1912.\n- On 2 December 1877, Samson et Dalila was first performed in Weimar at the Grossherzogliches Theater, now the Staatskapelle Weimar, in a German translation.\n- In 1877, Auguste von Müller originated the role of Dalila in the world premiere of Camille Saint-Saëns's Samson et Dalila.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c30175d3-255a-5b2d-aa98-b7b19b78cc85",
        "text": "Page: Auguste von Müller. Sentence: Auguste von Müller (1848-1912) was a nineteenth-century German operatic mezzo-soprano and actress.\nPage: Auguste von Müller. Sentence: She is best remembered today for originating the role of Dalila in the world premiere of Camille Saint-Saëns's \"Samson et Dalila\" in 1877.\nPage: Samson and Delilah (opera). Sentence: It was first performed in Weimar at the Grossherzogliches (Grand Ducal) Theater (now the Staatskapelle Weimar) on 2 December 1877 in a German translation.",
